# Purpose-Conditioned Agency Research Braid

The braid records why the same loop keeps reappearing across research
traditions, as the 2026-09-07 synthesis argued: cybernetics says agency needs
feedback; goal research says action sits inside hierarchies of means and
reasons; self-determination says the quality and ownership of motivation
matter; active inference says an intelligent next move can seek information
as well as outcomes; extended cognition says external structure can change
the cognitive work an agent can do; contemporary agent research says parts of
an agent's memory, workflow, tools, and code can be improved from experience.

The protocol's addition is that the objective, interpretation, evidence,
relationships, authority, and proof also need to be explicit and revisable.
That is `core/agency-interface.yawn`, and this braid is its supporting map,
not its authority.
